      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #8, 2026-08-06): 17 ⎕CR
      ⍝ (base64 -> byte vector) used to silently mis-decode malformed
      ⍝ input instead of rejecting it: '=' (RFC 4648's pad character)
      ⍝ was only ever checked at cols-2/cols-1 to derive the missing-byte
      ⍝ count, never validated as *invalid* everywhere else -- so a '='
      ⍝ as b1/b2 produced an out-of-range "byte" 256 (masked bits were
      ⍝ dropped for b3/b4 but not b1/b2), embedded padding ('QQ==QQ==')
      ⍝ silently decoded as zero bytes, and a stray '=' at cols-2 with a
      ⍝ non-'=' at cols-1 (e.g. 'AA=A') silently derived the wrong
      ⍝ output length. All four are DOMAIN ERROR now; well-formed input
      ⍝ (tested throughout this file) is unaffected.
      ⍝
      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR '=AAA'
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR '=AAA'
           ^  ^
      )SIC

      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR '===='
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR '===='
           ^  ^
      )SIC

      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR 'QQ==QQ=='
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR 'QQ==QQ=='
           ^  ^
      )SIC

      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR 'AA=A'
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕UCS 17 ⎕CR 'AA=A'
           ^  ^
      )SIC

