      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(h)): 43 ⎕CR (parse) of unparsable text
      ⍝ printed its DOMAIN ERROR twice and )MORE showed a raw numeric
      ⍝ ErrorCode. Source: the DOMAIN_ERROR inside the "if (ec)" branch
      ⍝ of do_CR42_43's parse path used to sit INSIDE the try block
      ⍝ that catches parser.parse()'s own exceptions, so its own throw
      ⍝ was immediately caught by that same catch clause, which then
      ⍝ built and threw a second DOMAIN ERROR describing the first.
      ⍝
      43 ⎕CR '(('
DOMAIN ERROR+
      43 ⎕CR '(('
      ^  ^

      )MORE
the parser returned error code: Unbalanced left parenthesis
      )SIC

      ⍝ A ⎕CR[X] B: user-defined boxing styles ----------------------------
      ⍝
      ⍝ A ⎕CR[⍬] B returns the 89 frame characters of boxing style A, and
      ⍝ A ⎕CR[X] B formats B like A ⎕CR B, but with the leading frame
      ⍝ characters of style A replaced by X. With X←A ⎕CR[⍬] B, both must
      ⍝ give the same result (this also caught 20-22 mapped to the wrong
      ⍝ styles).
      ⍝
      V←1 'ab' (2 2⍴⍳4)
